yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi no longer runs on claude-zzz. --model is now taken as the system prompt, and the request goes out on the default model. Before this, the request was sent on claude-zzz. Committed as fb0c95bf, titled "Part of #1114".

The fix: flag_value and flag_value_warning_for now find their flag with cli_config::option_position instead of args.iter().position(..). That function already skips the value of any earlier flag that takes one, and stops at a bare --. I reused it rather than writing a second copy, because every caller passes argv with the binary at index 0, which is what it expects. The fix sits at the one definition, so every caller gets it.

Who calls it (39 of 39 call sites, found by grep):
• 11 production calls in `cli.rs`: all pass option_args(full argv) from parse_args_with_config.
• 10 production calls in `dispatch_sub.rs`: all pass the full argv, with the subcommand at index 1 (doctor, version -v, review, resolve_api_key, and one other arm).
• 18 unit-test calls: every test argv starts with "yoyo".

Tests (3 new in tests/flag_value_slot.rs; they run the real binary against a local stub):
• The bug case: the request is not sent on claude-zzz, there's no unknown-model warning, and the system prompt is the literal --model.
• A plain --model claude-zzz still selects that model.
• The subcommand path is unchanged: yoyo version -v --model claude-zzz still prints model: claude-zzz.

Positive control: in one command I put the old lookup back (with a NEUTERED marker), ran the tests, then restored the fix. The first test failed by name (7 passed, 1 failed). After the restore, 8 of 8 passed and no marker was left.

Checks: cargo fmt, clippy -D warnings and the full cargo test run (7312 passed, 0 failed) are all clean. dispatch_sub.rs went from 2670 to 2677 lines, all doc comment, and its entry in tests/module_size.rs now carries the Day 252 reason.

Still open on #1114: collect_repeatable_flag and resolve_numeric_setting. I posted a comment on #1114 that leads with that scope, followed by the census.

One new problem I found and didn't fix: in that same command, the leftover word claude-zzz is now silently ignored, because -p already supplies the prompt. That's a different bug (an unused positional word gets no warning), so I noted it in the #1114 comment and didn't open a separate issue.
